{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie","id":124311,"title":"The Heart of Gaia movie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-02T23:14:35-07:00","id":124311,"title":"The Heart of Gaia movie","content":"Someone took the cutscenes of the failed game Werewolf the Apocalypse: Heart of Gaia and turned them into a full movie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bYmiwbO5icc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bYmiwbO5icc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bYmiwbO5icc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bYmiwbO5icc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Back then, it seems that White Wolf planned to have some White Howler remnants in the game by the way the plot sounded to me.<br /> <br /> What's your take on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T07:53:01-07:00","id":124490,"title":"","content":"It's a interesting watch. Reviving the White Howlers is a interesting concept for the video game, but how they did it would stay in the video game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T08:18:01-07:00","id":124512,"title":"","content":"Well I think that's a bit of a stretch. Had the game been released and treated as canon to some degree like the two VtM games were we would have had one pure breed White Howler out there who didn't really know jack all about his Tribe because there's no one left alive who knows much about the White Howler Tribe, their Gifts, their practices and their beliefs.<br /> <br /> Hell given the scene where Warsinger proclaims that Ryan will now be Ryan 'Dances-the-Spiral' I would say there would have been plenty of non-canon parts of that game had it been released.<br /> <br /> Though Phil Brucato did write a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/The_Heart_of_Gaia\" target=\"_blank\">ten part prequel story</a> to the game. And Ryan could have been an interesting means to explore the fallen Tribe in later books. That said I doubt we would have seen any other White Howlers.<br /> <br /> Of course with W20 out now and the upcoming White Howler Tribebook we do have the tools to change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T09:18:49-07:00","id":124554,"title":"","content":"Having been very farmiliar with this video for years, I gotta say its a mess. Let me list the ways it is messing itself;<br /> <br /> (note, I found this: <a href=\"http://pixelosity.net/werewolf/werewolfframeset.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://pixelosity.net/werewolf/werewolfframeset.html</a> site where the modeler has included his work. I take the names not said in the video from here)<br /> <br /> * GarouxGarou mating? The couple the priest tortured is hinted to be garou, as far as how I understood it.<br /> *War Singer of Black Furies, rank and auspice what? Yeah, I think the scripters had little experience with the game as WarSinger gives neither rank or auspice.<br /> * Raventongue's introducion is also weird 'I am the noble of the Shadow Lord garou'. It is clumsily worded, and just 'I am Adren of the Shadow Lords, punk!&quot; would have been better.<br /> * Dances the Spiral, to a White Howler bred cub, in front of Silver Fangs. Smart, WarSinger.<br /> <br /> Compared to the pretty well written VtM games that still kept the language correct (Bloodlines being better at it,though), this is one long trainwreck XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T12:42:25-07:00","id":124687,"title":"","content":"That's it? Honestly the possible Garou couple isn't that big a deal to me. If the Garou all rigidly clung to the Litany there wouldn't be any metis. Besides only the husband is confirmed Garou, we have no idea what the wife was before her death.<br /> <br /> As for Warsinger's introduction, even less of a deal than the above. As a player and ST of WtA I seldom give out formal introductions like that unless it's well... a formal situation. And that situation isn't that. The two were just fighting, Warsinger knows her caern is under attack and it's clear she realizes that Ryan is a mere pup and likely wouldn't understand rank and auspice.<br /> <br /> The script itself... yeah it could use some work. Some of the dialogue works but a good chunk of it is a mess. And when it boils right down to it the game's story as a whole suffers from Special Snowflake Syndrome, it is after revolving around playing as the last untainted White Howler. Now I don't have a problem with playing as the WH, in fact the first W20 game I ran involved modern day WH, or even the idea of the chronicle revolving around the only untainted Howler but rather my issue is with how they handled it as presented in these cutscenes. Admittedly we are miss one cutscene and any possible in-game dialogue but I doubt it would have made the story better. The things I particularly dislike about is the whole hunt for a magic McGuffin, prevent a plot to bring about the Apocalypse, storm a Pentex facility, send a young pup into the Black Spiral, while he's all more or less on his own. I have a similar issue with Bloodlines but that particular issue with that game is offset to a degree by the story which does do a good of giving the feel of being a neonate getting jerked around by their elders. At least until the later parts where it turns into a shooting gallery.<br /> <br /> Then again this was a game being made in the late 90's and would have been a 3rd person action game. Still it does make on wish for more video games with the CWoD IP. I love the VtM games and spent whole weekends doing four player co-op on the HtR games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T13:10:10-07:00","id":124711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124687#post124687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's it? Honestly the possible Garou couple isn't that big a deal to me. If the Garou all rigidly clung to the Litany there wouldn't be any metis. Besides only the husband is confirmed Garou, we have no idea what the wife was before her death.<br /> <br /> As for Warsinger's introduction, even less of a deal than the above. As a player and ST of WtA I seldom give out formal introductions like that unless it's well... a formal situation. And that situation isn't that. The two were just fighting, Warsinger knows her caern is under attack and it's clear she realizes that Ryan is a mere pup and likely wouldn't understand rank and auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem for that it feels less like it is because of the situations they are in and more from the ignorance of the creators. Granted, yeah, the wife might have been kin with gnosis. But when you have lines like 'Your garou name shall be Dances the Spiral' and 'I am a noble of the Shadow Lord garou', I'd say it was just the scripters not realising how an intro goes.<br /> <br /> Though, it is based on how I do it myself, so ^^''<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124687#post124687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The script itself... yeah it could use some work. Some of the dialogue works but a good chunk of it is a mess. And when it boils right down to it the game's story as a whole suffers from Special Snowflake Syndrome, it is after revolving around playing as the last untainted White Howler. Now I don't have a problem with playing as the WH, in fact the first W20 game I ran involved modern day WH, or even the idea of the chronicle revolving around the only untainted Howler but rather my issue is with how they handled it as presented in these cutscenes. Admittedly we are miss one cutscene and any possible in-game dialogue but I doubt it would have made the story better. The things I particularly dislike about is the whole hunt for a magic McGuffin, prevent a plot to bring about the Apocalypse, storm a Pentex facility, send a young pup into the Black Spiral, while he's all more or less on his own. I have a similar issue with Bloodlines but that particular issue with that game is offset to a degree by the story which does do a good of giving the feel of being a neonate getting jerked around by their elders. At least until the later parts where it turns into a shooting gallery.<br /> <br /> Then again this was a game being made in the late 90's and would have been a 3rd person action game. Still it does make on wish for more video games with the CWoD IP. I love the VtM games and spent whole weekends doing four player co-op on the HtR games.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Howlers seem to make writers both want to write a lot about them, but also make them seem like Snowflakes no one can play (before W20.) I think using a White Howler in the main role was not a good idea, as it removes the player character from the Nation, and from what I understand from the cut-scenes, Ryan's met only one Black Fury, some BSDs and the Fangs who all die. Even the neonate in Bloodlines had at least some contact to the other Kindred in the city, Ryan ends the game pretty much as confused about the Nation as he started. This essentially takes away huge part of the setting, and means the game never really goes beyond 'slay the Wyrm'. Having the PC be either a Fianna or a Get, or better yet, up to the player's pick, you'd have much easier time inserting the PC to the Nation.<br /> <br /> Though, to be honest, I think the script was in its very early drafts by that demo. Considering how stellar work both Hunter and Vampire had, I think if the game was ever finished I think the script would have been much more accurate.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T17:24:29-07:00","id":124866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124711#post124711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, to be honest, I think the script was in its very early drafts by that demo. Considering how stellar work both Hunter and Vampire had, I think if the game was ever finished I think the script would have been much more accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>What demo? Those are all but one of the games intended cutscenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T17:36:34-07:00","id":124876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124866#post124866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What demo? Those are all but one of the games intended cutscenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also lack any mouth movement, when as far as I know mouths could all ready move during cutscenes during that time. Considering how the whole thing is presented, it seems to me like a demo to the high ups in the company on what the game is going to be like. I have to check if its in this youtube video, but at the end of the one posted on megavideo, there was this 'coming (year)' text, hinting it was a preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T17:57:59-07:00","id":124883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124876#post124876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also lack any mouth movement, when as far as I know mouths could all ready move during cutscenes during that time. Considering how the whole thing is presented, it seems to me like a demo to the high ups in the company on what the game is going to be like. I have to check if its in this youtube video, but at the end of the one posted on megavideo, there was this 'coming (year)' text, hinting it was a preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that video is something a person made by combining the trailer they did for, which consists of that intro and ends with that same 'Coming 1999', and the 14 out of 15 cutscenes made for it. You can actually find all the individual cutscenes also on Youtube. Like the trailer here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MKWK-7YjScE\" data-code=\"MKWK-7YjScE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/MKWK-7YjScE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:13:49-07:00","id":124891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124883#post124883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually that video is something a person made by combining the trailer they did for, which consists of that intro and ends with that same 'Coming 1999', and the 14 out of 15 cutscenes made for it. You can actually find all the individual cutscenes also on Youtube. Like the trailer here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'll be. I thought it was the other way around, those clips from the presentation made into parts.<br /> <br /> Though, now I am surprised how lowgrade everything was, even for the times.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T12:42:03-07:00","id":125302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124891#post124891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, now I am surprised how lowgrade everything was, even for the times.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the era of the Unreal Engine. I still have the Next Generation magazine that talks about the game, you should see some of the other games in that issue (<i>I don't think Heart of Gaia was that low grade at the time if you looked at some of the other games.</i>). Plus the game wasn't even finished either.<br /> <br /> And if you wanted super special snowflake syndrome, you should read the W:tA novel, Call to Battle: The Saga of Jay No-Name by Doug Murray. Jay happens to be both a Garou and a Bubasti. And he can change into both forms...<br /> <br /> There was also another W:tA video game that became vaporware before this game too. Season of the Wolf was a game in development by Capcom because of the deal White Wolf used to have with them (<i>Game would be for the Playstation and the Sega Saturn</i>). Once Capcom and White Wolf went separate ways, that game became vaporware.<br /> <br /> There were aspects of Heart of Gaia mentioned in articles I was interested in, like the whole smell/scent mechanic in Lupus form. I haven't seen many games do something like that. Really bad games like, Dog's Life, just ruin it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T03:48:32-07:00","id":125695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"><