change into both forms...</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh yes, I am VERY farmiliar with Jay No-Name the orge cyborg cat. Interestingly enough, I think Jay and Ryan are related in that a lot of novel characters tend to become like them. There seems to be this love for the Howler tribe, as far as I've gotten from the first When Will You Rage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=125302#post125302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was also another W:tA video game that became vaporware before this game too. Season of the Wolf was a game in development by Capcom because of the deal White Wolf used to have with them (<i>Game would be for the Playstation and the Sega Saturn</i>). Once Capcom and White Wolf went separate ways, that game became vaporware.<br /> <br /> There were aspects of Heart of Gaia mentioned in articles I was interested in, like the whole smell/scent mechanic in Lupus form. I haven't seen many games do something like that. Really bad games like, Dog's Life, just ruin it.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ogyeHh0htKM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ogyeHh0htKM</a> This? Yeah, it looks interesting, and you have a choice on who you play as.<br /> <br /> I've seen the scent mechanic be used pretty nicely in a game. WolfQuest is a clumsy game, but it could scent mechanic pretty well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T15:05:36-07:00","id":126169,"title":"","content":"Some one needs to make GIFs out of those videos. VtM:Redemption was as terrible game (in all the right ways), but the Heart of Gaia video looks to be Grade A Cheese.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T10:20:00-07:00","id":129069,"title":"","content":"Watching this makes me so glad the game was never made.<br /> <br /> 90's Guy werewolf cub teams up with Fifty-Inch-Chest the Black Fury (She's a Black Fury! her girlfriend Karen was attacked!) to get the mcGuffin and stuff. They go to pentex! And he's a White Howler, because of his jeans! All in a graphics engine that makes Minecraft look high-res.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T11:57:02-07:00","id":1130917,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#313131\"> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">OK, I know that last post here was written almost 4 years ago, but I'm new here and I was watching the development of this game (and was very disapointed when it became clear that I will never play it). Few things I noticed on this video:<br /> <br /> 1. Warsinger - she's probably Galliard lupus. Her image and name resembles template from BF tribebook 1 ed.<br /> 2. Last of the White Howlers - according to WW, there are no White Howlers tribe because their totem is no more. But some of their kinfolk was assimilated by Fenrir and Fianna tribes. So it is possible that Ryan is a White Howler by genetics (in the cutscenes you can hear &quot;you carry the White Howlers gene&quot;).<br /> 3. Dances-the-Spiral - it is a great deed name. First of all you are the proof that in the Black Labirynth you have 3 not 2 choices, as it is stated on W20 Book of Wyrm: become Black Spiral Dancer, death or walk through it intact. Second if you are the only one, who done that you will become one of the greatest hero in garou nation. And also you should remember that there are many garou whose ancestors turn their hearts to the Wyrm. They will LOOOOVE someone, who is a living proof that their great grand parents failed. I used Ryan &quot;Dances-the-Spiral&quot; McCullough in my games and it was exactly as I said. Or it can also means that you fight the BSD with grace. About the names: my character's name (and my nickname here) means that during his Rite of Passage he broke free entire pack from BSD prison with his bare teeth, not that he is a chicken (in polish there are no such word play).<br /> <br /> I've also got two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Where is stated that this game ends in the Silver Fangs sept?<br /> \u200b2. Do you know something more about new Werewolf video game?<br /> 3. I know that this is other game but does somebody here know where (in which state if it was somewhere stated) lies Ashcroft from Hunter: The Reckoning video games? And does someone has a map of it? Because I love its history and I would like to send my PCs there and I would also like to compare this with my own vision. Thx in advance.<br /> <br /> And BTW, hello everybody <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br /> </span> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T07:09:14-07:00","id":1132595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1130917#post1130917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b2. Do you know something more about new Werewolf video game?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://aggrogamer.com/article/5841/E3-2017-Interview--Werewolf-The-Apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\">http://aggrogamer.com/article/5841/E...The-Apocalypse</a><br /> <br /> And yes, I would play the Heart of Gaia for years, just because its a legendary Werewolf the Apocalypse pc game, Idon't care if it is not canon story accurate, it's awesome because it is what it is.<br /> And yes, I await the new game in agony.<br /> And yes, you have one like from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:53:57-07:00","id":1132699,"title":"","content":"Well, IMHO, entire WoD is non canon. Examples?<br /> 1. You cannot be Mage and Werewolf at the same time.<br /> 2. 6th Maelstorm released Demons from Hell. In response God send Messengers and Imbued some people.<br /> 3. Most earth movers/inventors/killers were humans.<br /> <br /> And reality?<br /> 1. Samuel Haights - Mage/Werewolf/ghoul at the same time.<br /> 2. Imbued and Demons walked the Earth centuries before.<br /> 3. Rasputin was claimed by Malkavians, Followers of Set, Ventrue, Nosferatu, Shadow Lords, Mages and Puppeters. So who was he, really?<br /> <br /> But I think that this is the magic of WoD. There is no truth out there. Only half-truths and lies. And that's how I like it.<br /> <br /> Thx for interview and like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T17:55:24-07:00","id":1132863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1132699#post1132699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, IMHO, entire WoD is non canon. Examples?<br /> 1. You cannot be Mage and Werewolf at the same time.<br /> 2. 6th Maelstorm released Demons from Hell. In response God send Messengers and Imbued some people.<br /> 3. Most earth movers/inventors/killers were humans.<br /> <br /> And reality?<br /> 1. Samuel Haights - Mage/Werewolf/ghoul at the same time.<br /> 2. Imbued and Demons walked the Earth centuries before.<br /> 3. Rasputin was claimed by Malkavians, Followers of Set, Ventrue, Nosferatu, Shadow Lords, Mages and Puppeters. So who was he, really?<br /> <br /> But I think that this is the magic of WoD. There is no truth out there. Only half-truths and lies. And that's how I like it.<br /> <br /> Thx for interview and like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call that magic so much as it was clear evidence that the WoD was more of a toolbox than people might have thought. Or, if CoD is a toolbox, than WoD is a very tightly-built restrictive computer case that doesn't have room to have everything that could be on its board on all at once, but the surface looks really cool, so you do what you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T18:16:19-07:00","id":1132877,"title":"","content":"Actually <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a>, the Lion, the Totem of the White Howlers is alive but it's been diminished and is now apart of the Griffon's Brood while most of its Brood has either become corrupted and Wyrm-servants or disappeared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T04:58:22-07:00","id":1132966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1132863#post1132863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't call that magic so much as it was clear evidence that the WoD was more of a toolbox than people might have thought. Or, if CoD is a toolbox, than WoD is a very tightly-built restrictive computer case that doesn't have room to have everything that could be on its board on all at once, but the surface looks really cool, so you do what you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a big fan of CoD. It's too clear for my taste. On the other hand a good ST can use all the contraries from cWoD and you would not even notice they were there. My friend was so good. I'm not saying that in CoD it's impossible. I just don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T05:03:19-07:00","id":1132969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1132877#post1132877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a>, the Lion, the Totem of the White Howlers is alive but it's been diminished and is now apart of the Griffon's Brood while most of its Brood has either become corrupted and Wyrm-servants or disappeared.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's not the point. I meant that the Totem is too weak to support the tribe, so technically, for the tribe, is dead. But IMHO campaign from&quot;Rage across Australia&quot; gave Garou Nation hope. If they could bring back Rainbow Serpent back, maybe the same can be done with Lion and Turtle and tribes considered to be lost can be reviven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T06:33:12-07:00","id":1132996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1132969#post1132969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the point. I meant that the Totem is too weak to support the tribe, so technically, for the tribe, is dead. But IMHO campaign from&quot;Rage across Australia&quot; gave Garou Nation hope. If they could bring back Rainbow Serpent back, maybe the same can be done with Lion and Turtle and tribes considered to be lost can be reviven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lion is stronger then the other 2. He never went into slumber. I have always disliked how this totem was handled. Turtle went into slumber because not only did he lose his Garou tribe but also his Mokole varna as well. Rainbow Serpent wasn't the Bunyip tribes totem spirit, Bunyip was and after they died off he disappeared no mention of slumber. Yes Lion lost his garou kin but his Bastet kin were all still very much alive. So, unlike his other counterparts he still had a source of warship beyond Griffon pulling him into his brood. For a tribe on the return he should have plenty of strength to support them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T08:20:38-07:00","id":1133018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1132996#post1132996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lion is stronger then the other 2. He never went into slumber. I have always disliked how this totem was handled. Turtle went into slumber because not only did he lose his Garou tribe but also his Mokole varna as well. Rainbow Serpent wasn't the Bunyip tribes totem spirit, Bunyip was and after they died off he disappeared no mention of slumber. Yes Lion lost his garou kin but his Bastet kin were all still very much alive. So, unlike his other counterparts he still had a source of warship beyond Griffon pulling him into his brood. For a tribe on the return he should have plenty of strength to support them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touche. So, according to official storyline and Heart of Gaia game we have one pure White Howler and no kinfolk from that tribe. And an active, if weakened, totem. Interesting. Nowy it's time for Ryan to win totem support, claim some kinfolk either by charisma or force and reclaim his ancestor's land im Scotland. Some voice in my head tells me that will be a great story. Especially with an Earthbound used to be revered by Picts near BSD caern in the Highlands <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> BTW,<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I found list of gifts that was to be used within the game and if we assume that most gifts that an to average garou posess come from his tribe then Ryan will be Ragabash or Ahroun from Children of Gaia tribe. I also noticed that he was mentioned in W:tA revised quickstart in example of story as an Ahroun (name and description match).</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 08-23-2017, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T11:35:25-07:00","id":1133095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133018#post1133018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Touche. So, according to official storyline and Heart of Gaia game we have one pure White Howler and no kinfolk from that tribe. And an active, if weakened, totem. Interesting. Nowy it's time for Ryan to win totem support, claim some kinfolk either by charisma or force and reclaim his ancestor's land im Scotland. Some voice in my head tells me that will be a great story. Especially with an Earthbound used to be revered by Picts near BSD caern in the Highlands <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> BTW,<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I found list of gifts that was to be used within the game and if we assume that most gifts that an to average garou posess come from his tribe then Ryan will be Ragabash or Ahroun from Children of Gaia tribe. I also noticed that he was mentioned in W:tA revised quickstart in example of story as an Ahroun (name and description match).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We have more then that, as i have discussed over many other posts. We have the White Howler that is frozen in the ice somewhere Captain America style, who happens to have a personal totem that won't let him die. This gives us a possible tribal leader with ties to the old ways. We have the wraith of a White Howler lingering in the Shadowlands who has evaded capture from the BSD up until now. This gives us an uncorrupted Ancestor spirit. We also have a non-cannon character from the story Hell-Storm, Gabriel White. This is another pure breed white howler who is saved from dancing the spiral by none other then Samiel Haight who was in love with the character mother once upon a time. <br /> <br /> We also have a full gifts list and tribal totems available to us from before the fall. The 4 NPCs plus the players in a chronicle focused around the return could take one of the lesser totems that haven't been seen or have depleted power to support them until they get Lion back on their side. You can even use elements from Past Lives to send the characters back in time to live through the fall.<br /> <br /> So there are already a lot of elements already in cannon and supporting stories that could be used to justify their return. The fact that the BSD tribe still produces throwbacks from time to time could be seen as a sign of their bloodline refusing to die despite how long its been since they walked the earth. Their mission, easy enough, is to hunt and purify or kill their tribesmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T12:30:31-07:00","id":1133113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133095#post1133095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We have more then that, as i have discussed over many other posts. We have the White Howler that is frozen in the ice somewhere Captain America style, who happens to have a personal totem that won't let him die. This gives us a possible tribal leader with ties to the old ways. We have the wraith of a White Howler lingering in the Shadowlands who has evaded capture from the BSD up until now. This gives us an uncorrupted Ancestor spirit. We also have a non-cannon character from the story Hell-Storm, Gabriel White. This is another pure breed white howler who is saved from dancing the spiral by none other then Samiel Haight who was in love with the character mother once upon a time.<br /> <br /> We also have a full gifts list and tribal totems available to us from before the fall. The 4 NPCs plus the players in a chronicle focused around the return could take one of the lesser totems that haven't been seen or have depleted power to support them until they get Lion back on their side. You can even use elements from Past Lives to send the characters back in time to live through the fall.<br /> <br /> So there are already a lot of elements already in cannon and supporting stories that could be used to justify their return. The fact that the BSD tribe still produces throwbacks from time to time could be seen as a sign of their bloodline refusing to die despite how long its been since they walked the earth. Their mission, easy enough, is to hunt and purify or kill their tribesmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but I cannot agree with you. OK, there's one WH frozen and he could be reawakened. But as far as I know wraith is not the same that ancestor spirit. I read somewhere (if I'm rights it was one of W:tO books) that uncorrupted soul of garou cannot find themselves in the Shadowlands. Only garou touched by Wyrm can go there. So it isn't uncorrupted. As for Gabriel White it's the dumbest theory I've every read. &quot;You are son of BSD, but you weren't in the Black Labyrinth so you are a White Howler&quot;. Whaaaat??? So, going the same Path: Calley (from &quot;When will you Rage&quot;, but from different story) was a metis Born from BSD books but saved by Children of Gaia. Was he a WH too?<br /> <br /> I've got also a question: where did you find this WH wraith. I tried to find it but unsuccesful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 08-23-2017, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:00:57-07:00","id":1133153,"title":"","content":"Anything that is alive can find itself in the Shadowlands if it died with strong enough regrets. It just so happens that most of their regrets are because of their fall. The tale of Cororuc can be found in the W20 Umbra, pg 101 under White Howlers. He has even been purifying BSD who hunt him.<br /> <br /> I also forgot about the BSD that is currently floating in the silver lakes of Erebus. It says if he came out he might be the first of a new white howlers tribe or something else entirely. (Page 62-63, W20 Umbra)<br /> <br /> Yes, the story wasn't particularly the best written but it was ok. Any BSD with Pure Breed 5 is technically still born Pure, a sign is that they are born with pure white hair in their lupine form. There was and might still be a camp of BSD are like the Silver Fangs when it comes to their breeding, they just normally don;t let their pups get away.<br /> <br /> I don't think that Metis can have Pure breed, but if they can and Calley has pure breed 5, then yes, (s)he could be a White Howler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T16:28:55-07:00","id":1133209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133153#post1133153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that Metis can have Pure breed</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? We've had numerous examples that they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T16:35:42-07:00","id":1133211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133209#post1133209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? We've had numerous examples that they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was at work when i said that without my books in front of me. I thought it might have something to do with spiritual tie that is normally attributed to pure breed. I admit I wasn't sure and I was hoping someone would correct me if I was wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T18:21:25-07:00","id":1133241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124554#post124554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having been very farmiliar with this video for years, I gotta say its a mess. Let me list the ways it is messing itself;<br /> <br /> (note, I found this: <a href=\"http://pixelosity.net/werewolf/werewolfframeset.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://pixelosity.net/werewolf/werewolfframeset.html</a> site where the modeler has included his work. I take the names not said in the video from here)<br /> <br /> <b>* GarouxGarou mating? The couple the priest tortured is hinted to be garou, as far as how I understood it.</b><br /> *War Singer of Black Furies, rank and auspice what? Yeah, I think the scripters had little experience with the game as WarSinger gives neither rank or auspice.<br /> * Raventongue's introducion is also weird 'I am the noble of the Shadow Lord garou'. It is clumsily worded, and just 'I am Adren of the Shadow Lords, punk!&quot; would have been better.<br /> * Dances the Spiral, to a White Howler bred cub, in front of Silver Fangs. Smart, WarSinger.<br /> <br /> Compared to the pretty well written VtM games that still kept the language correct (Bloodlines being better at it,though), this is one long trainwreck XD</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there has to be a huge number of Garou shacking up to account for the hundreds of canonical Metis, even assuming they're the only ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T06:25:12-07:00","id":1133346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133153#post1133153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that is alive can find itself in the Shadowlands if it died with strong enough regrets. It just so happens that most of their regrets are because of their fall. The tale of Cororuc can be found in the W20 Umbra, pg 101 under White Howlers. He has even been purifying BSD who hunt him.<br /> <br /> I also forgot about the BSD that is currently floating in the silver lakes of Erebus. It says if he came out he might be the first of a new white howlers tribe or something else entirely. (Page 62-63, W20 Umbra)<br /> <br /> Yes, the story wasn't particularly the best written but it was ok. Any BSD with Pure Breed 5 is technically still born Pure, a sign is that they are born with pure white hair in their lupine form. There was and might still be a camp of BSD are like the Silver Fangs when it comes to their breeding, they just normally don;t let their pups get away.<br /> <br /> I don't think that Metis can have Pure breed, but if they can and Calley has pure breed 5, then yes, (s)he could be a White Howler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh, yes, I forgot about Cororuc. But &quot;(...) certain werewolves with Wyrm taint on them can become Restless Dead (...)&quot; - Buried Secrets p.27. So it is also possibile that he isn't so pure as anyone think.<br /> <br /> BSD in Erebus can be purified. But was he a WH before he was tainted? He could be corrupted as a member of any tribe. And I think that if the legend about purifing BSD in a Silver Lake (as far as I know noone knows for sure if it works, so I treat this as a legend) he will become Ronin, not a member of its former tribe.<br /> <br /> I think that the only way to restore WH is to be Ronin (and you have to &quot;carry the White Howler Gene&quot;, like Ryan or Gabriel) untill Lion accept you and others as followers, then reform a tribe. I know that it sounds like Skindancers II, but that's the way I like it. Or you can also defreeze Captain White Howler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T06:57:26-07:00","id":1133356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=124554#post124554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having been very farmiliar with this video for years, I gotta say its a mess. Let me list the ways it is messing itself;<br /> <br /> (note, I found this: <a href=\"http://pixelosity.net/werewolf/werewolfframeset.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://pixelosity.net/werewolf/werewolfframeset.html</a> site where the modeler has included his work. I take the names not said in the video from here)<br /> <br /> * GarouxGarou mating? The couple the priest tortured is hinted to be garou, as far as how I understood it.<br /> *War Singer of Black Furies, rank and auspice what? Yeah, I think the scripters had little experience with the game as WarSinger gives neither rank or auspice.<br /> * Raventongue's introducion is also weird 'I am the noble of the Shadow Lord garou'. It is clumsily worded, and just 'I am Adren of the Shadow Lords, punk!&quot; would have been better.<br /> * Dances the Spiral, to a White Howler bred cub, in front of Silver Fangs. Smart, WarSinger.<br /> <br /> Compared to the pretty well written VtM games that still kept the language correct (Bloodlines being better at it,though), this is one long trainwreck XD</div> </div> </div> </div>1. They are married. But they didn't say that they are metis parents. During my games garou married each other many times to avoid legal problems and to pay lower taxes (yes, garou sometimes pay taxes :P).<br /> 2&amp;3. There is no law that makes you present you with rank and even auspice. It's a tradition. Especially when you attack/defend the caern. Especially when the other garou is Ronin unproved by Rite of Passage/male Ronin unproved by Rite of Passage.<br /> 4. She didn't call him -ikhtya. And Dances-the-Spiral is a great deed name (see my first post).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T08:29:32-07:00","id":1133389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133346#post1133346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahhh, yes, I forgot about Cororuc. But &quot;(...) certain werewolves with Wyrm taint on them can become Restless Dead (...)&quot; - Buried Secrets p.27. So it is also possibile that he isn't so pure as anyone think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou ghosts are pretty much identical to normal ghosts, so as long as Willpower is greater than the Shadow's Angst, he wouldn't be that impure, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BSD in Erebus can be purified. But was he a WH before he was tainted? He could be corrupted as a member of any tribe. And I think that if the legend about purifing BSD in a Silver Lake (as far as I know noone knows for sure if it works, so I treat this as a legend) he will become Ronin, not a member of its former tribe.<br /> <br /> I think that the only way to restore WH is to be Ronin (and you have to &quot;carry the White Howler Gene&quot;, like Ryan or Gabriel) untill Lion accept you and others as followers, then reform a tribe. I know that it sounds like Skindancers II, but that's the way I like it. Or you can also defreeze Captain White Howler. </div> </div> </div>BSDs in Erebus could be purified... if they desired to be. The vast, overwhelming majority have no desire to be cleansed, however, so they just stay in the silver lake forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:11:50-07:00","id":1133407,"title":"","content":"I think I need to clarify that I am not saying that Gabriel or Ryan are White Howlers, they are Ronin and so would be the BSD if he can every fish himself out of the lakes. They are however genetically tied or could be (the Erebus floater) however to that Tribe and as such have the potential to resurrect the Tribe. Cororoc is not Taint, if he was then he would not be able to Purify the BSD that were after him. The fact that the book clearly states that purified ghost pack are White Howlers means that he is carrying on the traditions of his former tribe. Though he has no ancestral home for his spirit to reside, he is still an ancestor spirit.<br /> <br /> I don;t think Skin Dancer's II is that far fetch honestly. We have discussed this at length before on the forum but I am unable to find the post right now. You need some tie-in to the old ways of the tribe. This could be thawing out the Undying One or could be gaining Cororuc and his packs alliance. In truth, both would be best as they would give the players weight with Lion when they go to win his favor. What would make them different from the Skin Dancers is that there is a past that they are tied to and can pull from if they learned how to. Players could come from Fenrir or Fianna stock as well. Any pup of white howler linage that hasn't been accepted into a tribe could potential answer the call.<br /> <br /> I started working up something similar to a SAS storyline but never really finished it. White Howlers have always been an interest of mine since i start playing WTA in the late 90's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:17:55-07:00","id":1133410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133356#post1133356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. They are married. But they didn't say that they are metis parents. During my games garou married each other many times to avoid legal problems and to pay lower taxes (yes, garou sometimes pay taxes :P).<br /> 2&amp;3. There is no law that makes you present you with rank and even auspice. It's a tradition. Especially when you attack/defend the caern. Especially when the other garou is Ronin unproved by Rite of Passage/male Ronin unproved by Rite of Passage.<br /> 4. She didn't call him -ikhtya. And Dances-the-Spiral is a great deed name (see my first post).</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Why not just live with kinfolk if you want to stay in the city? But in any case, it just seemed a bit of a silly setting misunderstanding more than anything else.<br /> 3. Dances the Spiral, to me, is akin to naming a German Fenrir Goosesteps-for-Reich. Even if Warsinger didn't call him itkyah, the name has no subversive elements to it. Like Breaks the Spiral, Undoes the Spiral or Walks the Spiral Pure. Dances the Spiral, to a BSD purebred cub (remember, BSDs can be born with PB5 which is a WH throwback), is saying that he is forever tainted by the history of the tribe and amounted to nothing else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:40:45-07:00","id":1133423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133389#post1133389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou ghosts are pretty much identical to normal ghosts, so as long as Willpower is greater than the Shadow's Angst, he wouldn't be that impure, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, as long. I don't know if there are any stats for Cororuc. And if the Angst is greater...<br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]BSDs in Erebus could be purified... if they desired to be. The vast, overwhelming majority have no desire to be cleansed, however, so they just stay in the silver lake forever.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Well, I think that nobody has <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 08-24-2017, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T15:41:24-07:00","id":1133570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133410#post1133410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Why not just live with kinfolk if you want to stay in the city? But in any case, it just seemed a bit of a silly setting misunderstanding more than anything else.<br /> 3. Dances the Spiral, to me, is akin to naming a German Fenrir Goosesteps-for-Reich. Even if Warsinger didn't call him itkyah, the name has no subversive elements to it. Like Breaks the Spiral, Undoes the Spiral or Walks the Spiral Pure. Dances the Spiral, to a BSD purebred cub (remember, BSDs can be born with PB5 which is a WH throwback), is saying that he is forever tainted by the history of the tribe and amounted to nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Maybe to provoke some questions about interpretation of this part of Litany. Or maybe to get a green card fast when there were no kinfolk available.<br /> 3. I don't think that BSD with PB5 is always a throwback of WH. Maybe it's from a line of pure breed but fallen garou of other tribe. And remember that Ryan is from pictish descent. Spiral was sacred to them, Fianna still use spiral pattern in their tatoos and scars. I think that spiral came in very different colours, not only Black.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T16:20:16-07:00","id":1133580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133570#post1133570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Maybe to provoke some questions about interpretation of this part of Litany. Or maybe to get a green card fast when there were no kinfolk available.<br /> 3. I don't think that BSD with PB5 is always a throwback of WH. Maybe it's from a line of pure breed but fallen garou of other tribe. And remember that Ryan is from pictish descent. Spiral was sacred to them, Fianna still use spiral pattern in their tatoos and scars. I think that spiral came in very different colours, not only Black.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the games' rules, purebred BSD is always a WH throwback. As far as I know, BSDs literally cannot have PB unless its the full 5. But still, even if spiral was sacred then, the fact still remains that Ryan's family tribe fell and have gone by the BSD title for centuries. The name itself is tainted in a way, it now refers to those that have betrayed Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T19:24:07-07:00","id":1133628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133580#post1133580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the games' rules, purebred BSD is always a WH throwback. As far as I know, BSDs literally cannot have PB unless its the full 5. But still, even if spiral was sacred then, the fact still remains that Ryan's family tribe fell and have gone by the BSD title for centuries. The name itself is tainted in a way, it now refers to those that have betrayed Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use Golden Rule here: if a purebreed garou make heel turn its pure blood doesn't disappear. It only changes. And name cannot be tainted IMHO. It was given after many battles with BSD. Maybe with grace of a dancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 08-24-2017, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T22:45:18-07:00","id":1133675,"title":"","content":"So, first of all I'll open this post saying &quot;thank you&quot; to whoever upped that video. Yes, I can write it on youtube, but I still think that he deserves to be mentioned here too for his efforts.<br /> I was a teenager playing tabletop WtA when I heard that they were developing a PC Werewolf game, and it's hard to explain how excited I was: it was everything you always wanted, made with the best game engine availlable that would have allowed real-time shapeshifting, morphing the character model without using cheap tricks (Like Morrowind did, for exemple). This video allowed me to finally understand how the game would have been, and that's some closure to my curiosity, at least.<br /> <br /> But enough emotional rollercoasters.<br /> Using the White Howlers is not that absurd: it's just a single-player videogame, and even if the story makes you the whitest fly of the White Howlers it's not like it harms anyone. Having Gaia saved by the last of a fallen clan, the only Garou in history that dances the Black Spiral without falling to the Wyrm is surely an epic tale of redemption and heroism. That said, I'd really have liked a game more like Bloodlines, where you can pick your tribe and have an experience closer to the actual Werewolf world... and p.s.: that applies to the new Cyanide Werewolf game too, because being a Ronin isn't really a great start for a WtA fan.<br /> But who knows, maybe they did it to let you pick your side halfway through the game and make you play without all the needed background knowledge to be a proper Garou. We'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1130917#post1130917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> [COLOR=#313131] [FONT=Verdana<br /> 3. Dances-the-Spiral - it is a great deed name. First of all you are the proof that in the Black Labirynth you have 3 not 2 choices, as it is stated on W20 Book of Wyrm: become Black Spiral Dancer, death or walk through it intact. Second if you are the only one, who done that you will become one of the greatest hero in garou nation. A</div> </div> </div> </div>Surviving the Black Spiral is fine for a single player game, but in a Werewolf campaign the idea that you can't beat Malfeas'corruption feels much better. It's darker and more fitting to the Werewolf main theme: fight an impossible battle because it's a battle that it's worth fighting. In a properly made PC game, choosing to dance the Spiral should have corrupted your character and made him serve the Wyrm (therefore opening the &quot;evil&quot; route for the player), no matter how noble were the reasons for him to enter Malfeas in the first place. Also, I think that the only reason he managed to exit the Spiral unscathed was tied to the White Howler heritage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that the only way to restore WH is to be Ronin (and you have to &quot;carry the White Howler Gene&quot;, like Ryan or Gabriel) untill Lion accept you and others as followers, then reform a tribe. </div> </div> </div>Lion is part of the Griffin brood now and not an independent totem anymore. I doubt he would leave his servitude to re-create the fallen tribe, it would be dishonorable. But maybe Griffin can be persuaded to let him go, being the avenger of extinct species that he is... of course, it should be asked by a lupus Howler.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133389#post1133389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BSDs in Erebus could be purified... if they desired to be. The vast, overwhelming majority have no desire to be cleansed, however, so they just stay in the silver lake forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember something written in some Umbra guide (can't remember which one) saying that Chariss was secretly keeping a BSD in Erebus to see if he could be purified. It also mentioned that he had been there for five years already without showing any change and the Incarna herself didn't know how much time could it take, even assuming it possible in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T05:48:41-07:00","id":1133752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133675#post1133675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surviving the Black Spiral is fine for a single player game, but in a Werewolf campaign the idea that you can't beat Malfeas'corruption feels much better. It's darker and more fitting to the Werewolf main theme: fight an impossible battle because it's a battle that it's worth fighting. In a properly made PC game, choosing to dance the Spiral should have corrupted your character and made him serve the Wyrm (therefore opening the &quot;evil&quot; route for the player), no matter how noble were the reasons for him to enter Malfeas in the first place. Also, I think that the only reason he managed to exit the Spiral unscathed was tied to the White Howler heritage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Garou Nation history is full of heroes which were unjustly punished for their glorious deeds. For example Albrecht Morningkill: he killed dangerous bane terrorizing North Country Protectorate and was banished from the sept for that. Garou heroes were killed by their own kind for less. And in Heart of Gaia the choices made by player affected the ending (like in Jedi Knight). So this video shows only one version of the story. A propos the story: on white wolf wikia you can find story written by Paul Brucato and published before the game on press conferences to serve as &quot;prequel&quot; for the game. About darkness in p&amp;p Werewolf: I used the story from the game for one of my players. He went through the entire story more or less as it was shown in the cutscenes (so he went to Malfeas and lived to talk about it). And after that Ryan (I didn't change anything), as his character, was haunted by his own ancestor who was one of the first BSD (Adagach of the Balefires), hated by elder garou for showing them that surviving Malfeas is possibile, even without the pack (so they cannot scare cubs with it anymore) and was responsible for death and corruption of at least 4 cubs and younger garou who wanted to be like him and went to Malfeas alone. In the end the voices of Adagach and Alyn McCullough (son of Elyr McCullough and Adagach, then known as Clonach the White), last uncorrupted from his ancestors, became so loud that the player decided his character to commit suicide for fear of insanity and possibility of corruption. Dark enough?<br /> <br /> As for the story you can find it here: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/The_Heart_of_Gaia\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/The_Heart_of_Gaia</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 08-25-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T14:11:11-07:00","id":1134253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1133752#post1133752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> in Heart of Gaia the choices made by player affected the ending (like in Jedi Knight). So this video shows only one version of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you tell me where can I find about the multiple endings in Heart of Gaia ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T14:53:09-07:00","id":1134268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/124311-the-heart-of-gaia-movie?p=1134253#post1134253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you tell me where can I find about the multiple endings in Heart of Gaia ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't said straight. But I've played Jedi Knight and it have multiple ending so I assume that in Heart of Gaia they planned it the same way. You can find it here: <a href=\"https://www.unseen64.net/2016/10/10/werewolf-apocalypse-videogame-cancelled/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.unseen64.net/2016/10/10/...ame-cancelled/</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 08-26-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T15:22:19-07:00","id":1134279,"title":"","content":"Thank you very smooch sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T15:59:05-07:00","id":1134290,"title":"","content":"You're welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"